1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:03,983
Take a deep breath and hold it… What really happens inside your body?

2
00:00:05,250 --> 00:00:09,144
Surprise: the urge to breathe isn't mainly from low oxygen.

3
00:00:09,144 --> 00:00:11,586
It's from carbon dioxide building up.

4
00:00:12,290 --> 00:00:16,919
Sensors in your brainstem notice your blood getting more acidic and tell you: breathe!

5
00:00:18,290 --> 00:00:22,791
Soon your diaphragm, the breathing muscle under your lungs, starts twitching on its own.

6
00:00:24,290 --> 00:00:28,597
Your heart may also slow down, especially with your face in cold water.

7
00:00:28,597 --> 00:00:30,114
That's the diving reflex.

8
00:00:30,810 --> 00:00:36,015
On dry land, your brain usually forces you to take a breath long before it gets dangerous.

9
00:00:36,810 --> 00:00:41,003
But never breathe fast to prepare, or do breath-holding games underwater.

10
00:00:41,003 --> 00:00:43,530
You can black out without warning and drown.

11
00:00:44,230 --> 00:00:49,139
If someone passes out in water, get them out safely and call emergency services.

12
00:00:49,139 --> 00:00:50,182
Never swim alone.
